  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund: Libsense Activities in Nigeria, Sierra Leone and Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To replicate the positive impact of the LIBSENSE national open science symposiums in Nigeria and Sierra Leone with a focus on higher education and research institutions. These 2-day symposiums to convene stakeholders in Abuja and Freetown will build on the experience in Ghana and the other countries and aim to:
1.	Highlight the importance of open access/open science in achieving the SDGs and develop a shared vision for a national open science policy framework.
2.	Consult with diverse stakeholders and partners to understand the landscape and establish a priority-setting process.
3.	Identify opportunities for building synergies in the science, tech, and innovation ecosystem for open science.
4.	Co-create a road map for an enabling policy environment, including priority infrastructure and capacity building.
5.	Discuss the value of other quality assessment systems for scholarly journals and books, shifting from citation analysis-based evaluation in Indexing services from commercial companies to not-for-profit Indexing services.
For Ghana, to upskill University Librarians in Ghana on research data management topics.</narrative>
  </description>
